abulary then as i progress in a  language i do less and less of that and  more and more of my activity is simply  reading and listening and particularly  listening and that gets me to the poll  that i want to do today  i think listening comprehension is the  most important skill it's the  fundamental skill if we understand well  what we hear when people speak to us if  we watch movies if we listen to the  radio we listen to audio books we listen  to stories if we understand well we are  on our way to being able to speak it  means that we can hear clearly what is  being said we have sufficient vocabulary  we have sufficient familiarity with the  language we have the ability to  understand what we hear that's a  fundamental skill so what and i spend  most of i would say that um i probably  spent 70 percent of my time listening  maybe 25 percent of my time reading and  then the rest is on  possibly reviewing words or  looking things up in a grammar book or  googling for grammar information so  listening is absolutely key  i get in i think on average an hour a  day  between being in the car working out  cleaning up around the house and so  forth i get in an hour a day that's  theoretically seven hours a week  what i would like to ask is how much  time do you all spend listening all  right and there'll be four sort of  options those people who get in seven  hours a week an hour a day seven hours a  week or more that's category one  category two is people who get in let's  say half that let's say three hours  three to seven hours a week of listening  and then the next category three is  those who get between one hour to three  hours a week of listening in and  category four is people who do less than  one hour a week of listening i would  like to see where you all fit in in  these four categories so that's the poll  uh  look forward to your answers  and thank you for listening and if you  enjoy these podcasts please subscribe  bye for now  [Music]  you
 

